## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design a scalable, tenant-isolated CDC and schema evolution pipeline with robust governance, security, and rollback requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Change Data Capture (CDC) at cloud scale
- Per-tenant data isolation and architecture
- Schema drift detection and automated validation
- Backward-compatible migration strategies
- Data Catalog contract enforcement
- DLP-based PII masking and data protection
- Data Exchange for secure partner publishing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-logic: drift detection
function driftCheck(incomingSchema, currentSchema) {
  const changes = schemaDiff(incomingSchema, currentSchema);

  if (isBackwardCompatible(changes)) {
    generateMigration(changes);
    createSnapshot();
    applyMigration(changes);
  } else {
    alertSchemaViolation(changes);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cross-tenant streaming pipeline with privacy controls, data lineage, schema evolution, and disaster recovery in a production GCP environment.

## Key Concepts
- Dataflow streaming with per-tenant data routing and isolation
- BigQuery partitioned tables and multi-tenant architecture
- Data Catalog integration for end-to-end lineage tracking
- Cloud Run policy engine for tenant-specific data quality enforcement
- Schema registry and drift detection mechanisms
- Late data handling with event time processing and watermarks
- 24-hour rollback via BigQuery time travel or snapshot strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: tenant routing and masking in Dataflow
function processEvent(event) {
  const tenantId = event.tenant_id;
  const masked = maskPII(event); // DLP API or custom UDF
  return {
    tenant: tenantId,
    data: masked,
    timestamp: event.event_time,
    lineage: {pipeline: 'stream-analytics', source: 'pubsub'}
  };
}
